@startuml scanner_class
title plogic - Scanner stage

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class Orchestrator

enum TokenType {
  Not
  And
  Or
  Implication
  Biconditional
  Literal(bool)
  Identifier(str)
  LeftParen
  RightParen
  Newline
  Eof
  --
  +{static} map(lexeme: str): Result<TokenType, str>
}

class Token {
  +kind: TokenType
  +line: int
  +col: int
  +reserved_word: bool
  --
  +to_string(): str
}

class ScanState {
  -source: str
  -token_start: int
  -current: int
  -line: int
  -tokens: List<Token>
  -errors: List<Error>
}

class Scanner {
  +{static} scan(source: str): Result<List<Token>, List<Error>>
  -{static} scan_token(state: ScanState): ScanState
  -{static} match_char(state: ScanState, expected: char): (bool, ScanState)
  -{static} peek(state: ScanState): char option
  -{static} peek_next(state: ScanState): char option
  -{static} is_at_end(state: ScanState): bool
  -{static} advance(state: ScanState): ScanState
  -{static} add_token(state: ScanState, kind: TokenType): ScanState
}

enum Error {
  ScanError(line: int, col: int, message: str)
  ParseError(line: int, col: int, message: str)
  EvalError(message: str)
  --
  +to_string(): str
}

note bottom of Scanner
  Pure and never constructed: the immutable ScanState
  is threaded through every helper and returned anew.
  The state owns the source, so no helper carries a
  lifetime; the text is dropped with the state.

  Character handling:
  - spaces and tabs separate lexemes;
  - LF or CRLF emits Newline and advances line;
    a lone CR is an invalid character;
  - ! ¬ & ∧ | ∨ → ↔ are single-character lexemes;
  - -> and <-> are the only multi-character ones;
  - digit runs map to Literal(false) / Literal(true),
    any other run is a ScanError;
  - ASCII letter runs are words: reserved spellings
    map to their kind and set reserved_word, anything
    else is Identifier with reserved_word false.

  line and col are 1-based; col counts characters from
  the last line break, including a tab as one, and is
  derived, not stored. Errors are collected and the
  partial token list is discarded: Err(errors) or
  Ok(tokens).
end note

Orchestrator ..> Scanner

Scanner ..> ScanState : <<use>>
ScanState --> Token : tokens
ScanState --> Error : errors
Token --> TokenType : type

@enduml
